Upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp 4d71b42fd (#31179, "ggml-cpu : rewrite concat as one row kernel for all types"), MIT.
CPU concat split its work over dim 2 only, so a concat with ne2 == 1 (the FLUX single-block concat) ran on one
thread. One row kernel now covers every type and splits rows over all threads; dst bytes are the same copies.
Includes the upstream test-backend-ops cases (transposed b).

